                <invention-title lang="de">VERFAHREN, VORRICHTUNG UND SYSTEM ZUR POSITIONIERUNG ELEKTRONISCHER PREISSCHILDER</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="fr">PROCÉDÉ, APPAREIL ET SYSTÈME DE POSITIONNEMENT D'ÉTIQUETTE DE PRIX ÉLECTRONIQUE</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="en">ELECTRONIC PRICE TAG POSITIONING METHOD, APPARATUS, AND SYSTEM</invention-title>
            </bibliographic-data>
            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>The present disclosure provides an electronic price tag positioning method, apparatus and system. The method includes: generating a control instruction; transmitting the control instruction to an electronic price tag whose location is known and an electronic price tag whose location is unknown under the coverage of a base station through the base station; the electronic price tag entering an inspection time window according to a rule set by the control instruction, transmitting and receiving a signal according to a predetermined rule, and determining identities of surrounding electronic price tags according to the received neighboring price tag signal; receiving first identity information (its own identity information and identity information of other electronic price tags that are able to be received according to the control instruction) returned by the electronic price tag through the base station; determining a neighborhood relationship among the electronic price tags according to the first identity information; and determining location information of the electronic price tag whose location is unknown according to the neighborhood relationship and location information of the electronic price tag whose location is known. Through the technical solution, the location information of an electronic price tag whose location is unknown can be determined through a neighborhood relationship among the electronic price tags and the electronic price tags whose location are known, thereby improving the positioning accuracy.</p>
            </abstract>
